  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations through FY2027 to date total $4.7B. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $3.4B, making Veterans Affairs the single largest contracting agency in this partial-year snapshot. National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $354M, followed by the Department of the Treasury at $213M and the General Services Administration at $162M. The Department of Justice obligated $98.1M, the Department of Commerce obligated $92.1M, and the Department of Energy obligated $85.9M. The Department of Agriculture obligated $69.8M, the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $59.8M, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $58.1M. These ten agencies together represent the ranking of federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Contract totals are fiscal year to date and therefore partial for the current fiscal year. Use these figures as a snapshot of current federal buying patterns rather than full-year totals.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agency leads contract obligations in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs leads contract obligations with $3.4B. National Aeronautics and Space Administration is the next largest with $354M, followed by the Department of the Treasury with $213M. General Services Administration follows with $162M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How distributed are contract obligations across the top agencies?",
        "body": "Total federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date equal $4.7B. Nine other agencies have obligations ranging from $354M to $58.1M, including Department of Justice at $98.1M and Department of Commerce at $92.1M. These figures reflect partial-year obligations and represent the current distribution among the top ten contracting agencies."
      }
    ]
  },
